<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Concordat of Worms</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1122">1122</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Pactum Calixtinum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Concordat of Worms was the agreement of September 1122 between Emperor Henry V and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-callixtus-ii">Pope Callixtus II</a> that ended the Investiture Controversy. The emperor gave up investing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> with ring and staff, while in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> elections were to take place in his presence and he granted the elected bishop the regalia with a sceptre. It was concluded at Worms, one of the leading cities of the Salian emperors.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/concordat-of-worms.jpg" alt="Concordat of Worms" width="320" height="342" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown Original uploader was DALIBRI at de.wikipedia; derivative work by Saibo (Δ) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Urkunde_Wormser_Konkordat-bg.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
